After a long walk, my legs are tired.
I stop at a small café to take a break.
I go inside and over to the counter.
"Hi," I say to the man behind the counter.
"I would like a cup of coffee and a cinnamon roll, please."
He nods toward a free table.
"Sit by the window," he says.
I sit at the table with my food and coffee.
My cinnamon roll is still warm.
I take a bite and look out at the street.
